      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Cook and Housekeeper\u0027s Dictionary\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Mary Eaton (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#eaton-1822\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EEaton 1822\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E);",
      "receiptText": "OYSTER MOUTH SOUP. Make a rich mutton broth, with two large onions, three blades of mace, and a little black pepper. When strained, pour it on a hundred and fifty oysters, without the beards, and a bit of butter rolled in flour. Simmer it gently a quarter of an hour, and serve up the soup.\u003Cbr\u003E"
